------------Q3.Demonstrate and describe chmod, adduser, pwd commands.------------------ 
pwd (Present Working Directory):
It is used to display the current working directory path where the user is presently working.

chmod (Change Mode):
It is used to change the permissions of a file or directory such as read, write and execute.

adduser:
It is used to create a new user account in the Linux system.


