--------------Q5.Demonstrate cp command through system call. Describe respective commands.------- 
‘
Code:-
import os, sys

s=sys.argv[1]
d=sys.argv[2]

f1=os.open(s,os.O_RDONLY)
f2=os.open(d,os.O_CREAT|os.O_WRONLY|os.O_TRUNC,0o644)

while True:
    data=os.read(f1,1024)
    if not data:
        break
    os.write(f2,data)

os.close(f1)
os.close(f2)

print("File copied successfully")

Theory:-
import os, sys
• Imports required modules

s = sys.argv[1]
d = sys.argv[2]
• Reads source and destination filenames

os.open()
• Opens source and destination files

os.read(f1, 1024)
• Reads data from source file in blocks of 1024 bytes

os.write(f2, data)
• Writes data into destination file

os.close()
• Closes both files after copying

print("File copied successfully")
• Displays success message


-----------------Q6.Demonstrate and describe process related commands. -------------------
Theory :-
#!/bin/bash
• Executes script using bash shell

ps
• Shows current running processes

ps -ef
• Displays all processes with details

sleep 60 &
• Runs process in background

jobs
• Shows background jobs

kill %1
• Kills background job

CODE:

#!/bin/bash

echo "Process Commands"

echo "1. Current Processes"
ps

echo "2. All Processes"
ps -ef

echo "3. Top CPU Processes"
ps -e -o pid,pcpu,comm --sort=-%cpu | head

echo "4. Background Process"
sleep 60 &
jobs

echo "5. Kill Background Process"
kill %1
jobs

